# One 60-ply game, as long-algebraic moves, replayed move by move by `cargo xtask warm-ab`.
#
# The AXIS, not a golden: nothing here is compared against upstream. What the file has to be
# is FIXED, because a warm replay's node total is a function of the move list and the table
# alone, and two revisions that search the same tree must report the same total. A run whose
# totals differ is VOID rather than slow.
#
# Produced by this engine playing itself at `go depth 12`, Hash 16, Threads 1, from the start
# position -- a real game rather than a position list, because the regime being measured is a
# search that INHERITS a filled transposition table and populated history banks. `bench` is
# the opposite: a cold search of an unrelated position, and it is a different workload. At
# depth 12 over these plies this port searches 728,110 nodes warm and 1,424,756 cold.
#
# Moves are read in order and the comment lines are stripped before the script is piped, so
# unlike a `.uci` fixture a `#` line here is a comment and not a command.
e2e4 e7e5 g1f3 b8c6 f1b5 a7a6 b5a4 g8f6 e1g1 f6e4 d2d4 b7b5 a4b3 d7d5 d4e5 c8e6
